  "request": {
    "spec": "Each person's row gains a statement button. Taking a statement records the person's due-total at\nthat moment (STATEMENT name=<name> due-total=<due-total> claims=<count of their claims that\ncount>), and binds every claim of theirs that counts at that moment to the figure it has then:\nfrom now on that claim shows and totals that bound figure, whatever later changes to rates or\ngrades would have made it, until the person's next statement rebinds all their counting claims\nto their figures as of that moment. A claim of theirs that does not count at a statement is left\nunbound (live again). A settled claim's frozen figure is unaffected. Show on each claim stated\nyes/no, and on the person their statement count, the last statement's due-total and its date\n(the sheet's today when it was taken).\n",
    "prompt": "You are implementing ONE change to this application.\n\nFIRST read AGENTS.md \u2014 it states the working rules and how the app is tested, and sends you to\nDESIGN.md for the app's stack and conventions. Follow both.\n\nTHE CHANGE REQUEST:\nEach person's row gains a statement button. Taking a statement records the person's due-total at\nthat moment (STATEMENT name=<name> due-total=<due-total> claims=<count of their claims that\ncount>), and binds every claim of theirs that counts at that moment to the figure it has then:\nfrom now on that claim shows and totals that bound figure, whatever later changes to rates or\ngrades would have made it, until the person's next statement rebinds all their counting claims\nto their figures as of that moment. A claim of theirs that does not count at a statement is left\nunbound (live again). A settled claim's frozen figure is unaffected. Show on each claim stated\nyes/no, and on the person their statement count, the last statement's due-total and its date\n(the sheet's today when it was taken).\n\nYour work is verified by an automated Playwright UI test already installed under e2e/specs/.\nRead that spec: it declares the exact data-testid anchors, values, test data and any audit\nrecords it expects \u2014 match them. Run `bin/e2e` to build the app, start it, and run the test as\nyou work; iterate until it passes. Change whatever the request needs across the app \u2014 its stored\ndata, its server and its front end. Do NOT edit bin/build, bin/start, bin/stop, bin/e2e,\nAGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, DESIGN.md, e2e/support/ or the test spec.\n"
  },
