    "result_text": "I added the statement feature and all 4 Playwright tests in `bin/e2e` pass on the first run.\n\n**What it does**\n- **Statement button:** each person's row now has a statement button. Pressing it works out the person's due-total right then and writes `STATEMENT sheet=\u2026 by=\u2026 name=\u2026 due-total=\u2026 claims=\u2026` to the audit file.\n- **Binding:** every claim of theirs that counts (OPEN or SETTLED) is fixed at the figure it has at that moment. From then on it shows and adds up that figure, even if rates or the person's grade change. The person's next statement fixes their counting claims again at the new figures. Any claim that doesn't count at that point goes back to being live.\n- **Settled claims:** a settled claim keeps its settled figure; a statement never changes it.\n- **On screen:** each claim shows Stated yes/no. Each person shows how many statements have been taken, the last one's due-total, and its date (the sheet's today when it was taken). The last two are blank until the first statement.\n\n**Changes by layer**\n- **Stored data:** a new migration, `V12__statement.sql`, adds `stated` and `stated_due` to claims, and the statement count, last due-total and date to people.\n- **Server:** a new endpoint, `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/people/{personId}/statement`, made of three steps (`TakeStatement`, `AuditStatement`, then the existing `RespondWithPerson`). Taking a statement doesn't change the person's version number, so it won't make someone else's open edit form get refused as out of date.\n- **Front end:** `Claims.tsx` uses the fixed figure when a claim has one. `People.tsx` has the new `PersonStatement` cell. A refused statement shows the row's `person-error`.\n\n**Three decisions the request didn't settle, and the tests don't check:**\n- **Settling a stated claim** fixes it at its stated figure, not at the current rate, so its number doesn't jump when it's settled.\n- **No rate at statement time:** a claim with no rate is still marked stated, and its figure is n/a.\n- **When a due-total shows n/a:** it already showed n/a if the person's grade has no rate today, unless a counting claim has a settled figure. A stated figure now counts as well.",
